  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 with multiprofile+avgpool (config_005, acc=0.650) is the current best RNA-only configuration, and multiprofile+aggregation is clearly beneficial over singleprofile. However, we have not yet tested the scgpt encoder, which is a fundamentally different RNA representation (foundation-model pretrained vs. variational autoencoder). Question: config_008 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) is a controlled comparison to config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) — only the RNA encoder changes, isolating its effect. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It directly resolves whether the top RNA encoder is scvi_n200 or scgpt, which is the single most consequential remaining design choice in the RNA pipeline before investing in multimodal fusion experiments. (2) The result will determine which encoder to pair with image modalities in subsequent multimodal trials, avoiding wasted budget on a suboptimal encoder. (3) It is a clean one-variable comparison, maximizing information per experiment under the limited budget."
